  "name": "Gendang lima sendalanen (Karo Batak ensemble)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Principal ensemble of the Karo Batak of the North Sumatran highlands, whose name means 'five instruments in one ensemble': the sarune double-reed shawm, two small double-headed drums beaten with sticks, the gendang singanaki and singindungi (the generic membrane-drum card stands in), and two gongs, the small penganak and the larger gung. It accompanies dancing at guro-guro aron youth festivities, weddings, funerals and spirit rites; a smaller ensemble built around the keteng-keteng bamboo tube zither is a related form.",
